    "stepGroups": [
      {
        "id": "step-group-1",
        "name": null,
        "steps": [
          {
            "id": "step-1",
            "text": "Before starting, wash and dry all produce. Peel, then cut carrot into 1/4-inch half-moons. Cut bok choy into 1-inch pieces. Pat chicken dry with paper towels, then cut into 1-inch pieces. Sprinkle half the Moo Shu Spice Blend over chicken, then season with salt and pepper.",
            "durationMinutes": null,
            "durationMinutesMax": null,
            "temperature": null
          },
          {
            "id": "step-2",
            "text": "Heat a large non-stick pan over medium-high heat. When hot, add peanuts to the dry pan. Toast, stirring often, until golden, 2-3 min. (TIP: Keep your eye on peanuts so they don't burn!) Transfer to a plate.",
            "durationMinutes": 2,
            "durationMinutesMax": 3,
            "temperature": null
          },
          {
            "id": "step-3",
            "text": "Add 1 tbsp oil to the same pan, then chicken. (NOTE: Don't overcrowd the pan; cook chicken in 2 batches for 4 ppl, using 1 tbsp oil per batch.) Cook, stirring occasionally, until golden and cooked through, 4-5 min. Transfer chicken to a plate. Meanwhile, add 10 cups water and 1 tbsp salt to a large pot (use same for 4 ppl). Cover and bring to a boil over high heat.",
            "durationMinutes": 4,
            "durationMinutesMax": 5,
            "temperature": null
          },
          {
            "id": "step-4",
            "text": "Reduce heat to medium, then add carrots to the same pan. Cook, stirring often, 1-2 min. Add bok choy. Cook, stirring often, until veggies are tender-crisp, 1-2 min. Add chicken, vegetarian oyster sauce, honey-garlic sauce, 1/4 tsp (1/2 tsp) sugar, 2 tbsp (4 tbsp) water and remaining Moo Shu Spice Blend. Cook, stirring often, until sauce thickens, 2-3 min. Remove from heat.",
            "durationMinutes": 5,
            "durationMinutesMax": 7,
            "temperature": null
          },
          {
            "id": "step-5",
            "text": "Meanwhile, add noodles to the boiling water. Cook uncovered, until tender, 1-2 min. Drain noodles, then rinse under warm water. Drain well, then return to the large pot.",
            "durationMinutes": 1,
            "durationMinutesMax": 2,
            "temperature": null
          },
          {
            "id": "step-6",
            "text": "Add half the peanuts and stir-fry mixture to the pot with noodles. Toss to combine. Divide noodles between bowls. Sprinkle remaining peanuts over top.",
            "durationMinutes": null,
            "durationMinutesMax": null,
            "temperature": null
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
